# Factory runtime/generated artifacts are local by default (ACT-CLINEMM-FORK-BASELINE01).
# NOTE: Git cannot re-include a file when its parent directory itself is excluded,
# so the .factory directory must remain traversable and only its contents ignored.
# The canonical epic board is the exception and is durably tracked below.
# See ACT-CLINEMM-FACTORY-BOARD-DURABILITY-AND-FACTORIZE-INTAKE01.
/.factory/*
!/.factory/epic-board.md
# ACT-CLINEMM-FACTORY-EPIC-BOARD-SHARDING01: per-epic detail files under
# .factory/epics/ are durable, linkable substrate of the board architecture.
# See docs/factory-migrations/ACT-CLINEMM-FACTORY-EPIC-BOARD-SHARDING01-manifest.md.
!/.factory/epics/
# ACT-CLINEMM-TOOL-EXECUTION-SEMANTICS-IMPLEMENTATION01 (TES-IMPL-01): the
# implementation ACT contract is referenced from durable board and epic
# files, so the ACT itself MUST be durable (otherwise the canonical link
# would be broken on a fresh clone). Parked / waiting-for-evidence ACTs
# stay local — they have no durable binding contract yet.
#
# Policy: DEFAULT-DENY + WHITELIST. The `.factory/acts/` directory
# itself is re-included so git can recurse, but every file *under* it
# is ignored unless explicitly whitelisted below. This is forward-safe:
# any new file dropped under `.factory/acts/` (a future debug dump, a
# scratch ACT, a captured secret-bearing log) is local-by-default
# without needing to update this gitignore first. The policy contract
# is the gitignore rule itself, not a maintained inventory of known
# local-only filenames.
!/.factory/acts/
/.factory/acts/*
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-TOOL-EXECUTION-SEMANTICS-IMPLEMENTATION01.md
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-TERMINAL-REPORT-COMPLETION-FRAMING01-CORRECTION01.md
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-PTAD-ENV-OPTIN01.md
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-COMPLETION-PROTOCOL-LIVENESS02.md
!/.factory/acts/ACT-CLINEMM-SEATBELT-YOLO-COMPLETION-AUTHORITY-CONTRACT01.md

# Same principle for nested Factory state under apps/vscode (ACT-CLINEMM-DOGFOOD-BUILD-EVIDENCE-IGNORE01).
# apps/vscode/.factory/evidence/ holds generated local evidence from dogfood / seatbelt
# qualification runs and must NOT block exact-head VSIX packaging (build-dogfood-vsix.py
# runs `git status --porcelain=v1 --untracked-files=all` and HALTs on any ?? entry).
# The repo-root /  .factory/* rule above only matches paths whose first component
# is `.factory/`; Git's anchoring in /.factory/* means `apps/vscode/.factory/...`
# is NOT covered by it, so this symmetric rule is required.
apps/vscode/.factory/evidence/

# Factory staging/backup siblings (µC-3 round 6 atomic publish)
.factory-staging-*
.factory-backup-*

# Factory staging/backup siblings (µC-3 round 7 atomic publish)
.factory-leamas-staging-*

# Python build artifacts (ACT-CLINEMM-REPRODUCIBLE-DOGFOOD-VSIX01)
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
